Ohle Claussen schrieb:
> 
> On 2006-11-21, jaina@magic.ms wrote:
> > The one thing I don't know yet _and_ can't seem to find out by research
> > in spoilers or this group is:
> > Why are people wishing for "fixed rings"? Wishing for fixed items seems
> > to be the generic way to get fooproof armor and weapons, but on most
> > items the meaning is not clear to me.
> 
> You can wish for fixed anything. I believe that when doing this, the
> "fixed" bit of the object structure might actually be set, even if it is
> never queried in the source for rings. In other words, it's possible to
> get fixed rings from wishing, but the fixing doesn't do anything.

Rings can be rust- or fireproof. You're quite right - it's not an
important property: rings will only rust, and only when you take a
dive with them in your inventory; and such rusting will not make the
rings less useful.

*proofing _might_ protect rings from being eaten by xorns, rust
monsters, rock moles and possibly gelatinous cubes. Still rather
unimportant.

